properties.description:
Planned 2026-10-07, next build after #696. The served root-cause skill gains a neighbours pass, used whenever the design names member designs (its pins with a graph_id) or the session reaches several designs:
- step 2 searches past causes in every member;
- a CHANGE-ACROSS bone uses upstream_status, or each member's changelog where it is hosted, to name the members that moved since this design last looked;
- a SEAM bone compares the interfaces this design uses or provides with the member's current version (mirrored interfaces, seam_report);
- a RIPPLE-BACK bone runs propagate_from with arriving_from from each member that moved, to see whether the change reaches the failing part;
- a member it cannot reach is named as not looked at.
The /hub skill separates where to LOOK (the whole family) from where to RECORD (the design where the cause lives, with the symptom's design linking to it). Mostly skill text, plus a test that both skills carry the steps. Compounding across designs (budgets and tolerances rolled up across the family) is NOT in this: req:a-quantity-that-compounds-across-designs-is-rolled-up-across-the-family, deferred.



AS BUILT 2026-10-07:
- root-cause step 2 searches every member design, and names one it could not reach as not looked at.
- Step 3 gains a NEIGHBOURS pass of three bones (Change across: upstream_status, or changelog_view where hosted; Seam: the mirrored interface against the member's own; Ripple back: propagate_from with arriving_from). It names the compounding shape (budgets and tolerances across designs) as out of reach.
- Step 8 records the cause in the design where it lives, with a pointer from the symptom's design.
- The hub skill's routing section says where to record is not where to look.
The .claude and .grok mirror copies follow; skill_lint learned `members`. The pointer from the symptom to a cause in another design is text until the cross-design link (build order 4) exists.
